  "text": "Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY-U / PMAY-G) Operational Guidelines\n\nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (PMAY) Housing Guidelines\n\n1. Mission Objective\n\nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana addresses urban and rural housing shortages among Economically Weaker Sections (EWS), Low Income Groups (LIG), and rural homeless households by ensuring a pucca house with basic amenities to all eligible families.\n\n2. Eligibility Criteria\n\nThe beneficiary family should not own a pucca house anywhere in India.\n\nEconomically Weaker Section (EWS) annual household income up to Rs 3,00,000.\n\nLow Income Group (LIG) annual household income between Rs 3,00,001 and Rs 6,00,000.\n\nMiddle Income Group (MIG-I & MIG-II) income bands as notified by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs.\n\n3. Subsidy and Financial Assistance\n\nCredit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS) provides upfront interest subsidy of up to 6.5% on home loans up to Rs 6,00,000 for a tenure of 20 years. Rural beneficiaries under PMAY-G receive direct construction assistance of Rs 1,20,",
