  "text": "NATIONAL SOCIAL ASSISTANCE PROGRAMME (NSAP)\nINDIRA GANDHI NATIONAL OLD AGE PENSION SCHEME (IGNOAPS) GUIDELINES\n\n1. Background and Purpose:\nThe Indira Gandhi National Old Age Pension Scheme (IGNOAPS) is a non-contributory pension scheme under the Ministry of Rural Development aimed at providing monthly financial assistance to senior citizens living Below Poverty Line (BPL).\n\n2. Eligibility Conditions:\n- The age of the applicant must be 60 years or higher.\n- The applicant must belong to a household living Below Poverty Line (BPL) according to criteria prescribed by the Government of India.\n- Permanent residence certificate and active bank account seeded with Aadhaar are mandatory.\n\n3. Scale of Financial Assistance:\n- For persons aged 60 to 79 years: Central assistance of Rs 200 per month per beneficiary (States supplement this with an additional state share, making the total pension between Rs 1,000 to Rs 2,500 per month).\n- For persons aged 80 years and above: Central assistance of Rs 500 per month per beneficiary.\n\n4. Application and Verification:\n- Applications can be submitted online via the NSAP portal (https://nsap.nic.in) or offline through",
